#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1023 expect=skipped domain=LB
#note "⚠ RE-CUT 2026-09-08 (R-4.12 hoist): expect moved noViolation -> skipped. `var_exists(TV.VISIT)` was a top-level conjunct, so an absent TV made the whole AND false and the rule reported a SILENT ZERO -- which is what this scenario used to pin. It is now Requirements.Variables.All ["TV.VISIT"], so the rule is gated out and reports SKIPPED naming the variable. Same violations either way; only the status channel moves, which is R-4.11's whole argument. If this EXECUTES again the entry was dropped -- escalate, do not rewrite the pin. PRIOR NOTE: CL-G.1 / EC-82 option (a) (wave TA-4): PMDA-SD1023 completes the Fix #246 family. TV is absent entirely, so $tv_visit_keys is the empty set and the vacuous-on-empty membership would be true on every row with a populated (VISIT, VISITNUM) - the flood EC-82 records. The top-level var_exists(TV.VISIT) guard, now byte-identical with FDA-SD1023's, resolves TV through the dataset resolver, finds nothing, and suppresses the rule with no finding. ⛔ CORRECTED 2026-09-22: a paragraph appended here claimed "every primary row takes the `not SV._matched_` tier and is decided by the VISIT name". Untrue in THIS file — it is expect=skipped, so NO row is evaluated at all. The boilerplate was appended to all eight SD1023 fixtures without checking which of them actually execute. The SV block below is here only to satisfy Requirements.Datasets: [SV]; the skip is caused by the MISSING TV.VISIT, and that is what this file pins. ⚠ It now has two independent skip causes and pins neither by name."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset LB label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 1 | ALB | 2  | BASELINE
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 2 | ALB | 99 | WEEK 99
---

dataset SV label="Subject Visits"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | SV | 01-701-9999 | 1 | SCREENING
---
